 9 |     for $x in std::coll::list.from([1, 2], alloc: Lend $heap):
   |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 what: this fresh list grows on the heap, so it has to end with `done`, which a loop over it can't do
 why:  a loop over a fresh collection takes no word, and one that owns memory is stored first, read with `Lend` and ended with `defer` (D396, D325)
